% Amazing Grace: lead sheet engraved for pianist's sample (CC0). Melody "New Britain" (1829) and words (John Newton, 1779)
% are in the public domain; the chord symbols are this arrangement's own. Rebuild: abcm2ps -v -O sheet sheet.abc,
% then rsvg-convert -f pdf -o sheet.pdf sheet001.svg
X:1
T:Amazing Grace
C:Words: John Newton (1779)
C:Melody: New Britain (1829)
M:3/4
L:1/8
Q:1/4=80
K:G
%%gchordfont Helvetica 13
D2 | "G"G4 BG | "G7"B4 A2 | "C"G4 E2 | "G"D4 D2 |
"G"G4 BG | "Em"B4 A2 | "D"d6- | "D7"d4 B2 |
"G"d3 B dB | "G7"G4 D2 | "C"E3 G GE | "G"D4 D2 |
"Em"G4 BG | "D7"B4 A2 | "G"G6- | "G"G4 |]
W:1. Amazing grace! how sweet the sound
W:   That saved a wretch like me!
W:   I once was lost, but now am found,
W:   Was blind, but now I see.
W:
W:2. 'Twas grace that taught my heart to fear,
W:   And grace my fears relieved;
W:   How precious did that grace appear
W:   The hour I first believed!
